# Metric health and propagation foundation

Status: **Phase 006 is active. Groups 01–03 are accepted with HLTH-001–HLTH-029. Group 04 is next.**

Preserve permanently:

- successful load/run ≠ healthy produced table;
- available statistic ≠ useful metric;
- metric definition ≠ metric Observation ≠ Assessment;
- metric existence ≠ normative threshold;
- threshold authority ≠ metric statistical meaning;
- Baseline range ≠ normative Expectation;
- Observation ≠ reference-set membership ≠ Baseline summary/version ≠ comparative Assessment;
- local metric ≠ propagated metric ≠ derived reconciliation expectation;
- technical metric view ≠ separate business truth;
- upstream anomaly ≠ downstream failure;
- metric used for monitoring ≠ automatically safe for Execution Gate control;
- richer/expensive metric ≠ synchronous production-path requirement;
- semantic applicability ≠ profile selection ≠ source support ≠ current availability ≠ health outcome;
- `not applicable`, `not selected`, `unsupported`, `unavailable`, `pending`, and `pass` are distinct;
- same metric display name ≠ same definition/version when formula/denominator/grain/population semantics materially change;
- producer physical schema ≠ consumer-visible interface schema;
- structural compatibility ≠ Baseline/statistical comparability;
- available history ≠ eligible reference history;
- raw non-comparability ≠ derived normalized non-comparability when an explicit valid normalization exists;
- within Baseline ≠ healthy; outside Baseline ≠ failed/degraded.

Accepted Phase 006 Group 01 foundation:

- Define purposeful per-asset metric profiles rather than calculating every possible statistic.
- Distinguish core operational/table, critical-field/business, transformation-specific reconciliation, and diagnostic/on-demand profile roles.
- Canonical metric families are operational/output, temporal/freshness, structural/schema, volume/population, completeness/missingness, uniqueness/key integrity, validity/domain, distribution/shape, relational/transformation integrity, and business-semantic measurement.
- Metric applicability depends on semantic role, data type, grain, transformation, criticality/context, consumer use and definition version.
- Avoid meaningless metrics such as quantiles for opaque identifiers or universal column-level statistics without an identified failure mode/use.
- Material metric/check Observations retain definition/version, subject/window/grain/population, source/input evidence, temporal provenance, approximation/sampling/coverage limitations and restriction status.
- Diagnostic/on-demand evaluation does not automatically promote a metric to routine profile membership.

Accepted Phase 006 Group 02 structural foundation:

- Bind compatibility to the consumer-visible interface/contract and version, not merely producer physical DDL.
- Preserve declared/governed schema meaning, structural Expectation, proposed/planned state, realized Observation/Change, and compatibility Assessment as distinct.
- Add/drop/rename/reorder/type/precision/nullability/default/generated/key/grain/nested changes remain independently representable.
- Rename identity requires evidence; drop/add coincidence is insufficient.
- Additive/removal/type compatibility is consumer-specific and directional where applicable.
- Engine cast ability is not proof of compatibility.
- Key/grain changes can invalidate selected metric/Baseline/join assumptions without automatically constituting a defect.
- Pre-deployment validation success is not proof of realized production state.
- Structural change triggers scoped metric/Baseline review rather than global reset.
- `Compatible` requires sufficient evidence coverage of the bound contract; missing evidence is not compatibility.
- Structural incompatibility does not prove execution failure, exposure, Impact or causality.
- Validation placement remains deferred.

Accepted Phase 006 Group 03 Baseline/statistical foundation:

- Baseline reference membership/window/regime/calendar/cohort/definition/grain/interface semantics are explicit and provenance-bearing.
- Comparability is multidimensional and conclusion-relative; do not introduce a universal comparability/confidence score.
- Fixed, rolling, seasonal/cadence, cohort and post-change Baselines are functional reference classes, not algorithms.
- Recency does not override comparable calendar/cohort context.
- Realized semantic/structural/method breaks segment affected references only; new regimes derive from realized evidence rather than targets.
- Reference sufficiency depends on the intended claim; no universal sample minimum exists.
- Preserve denominator/population size and coverage; low-volume evidence limits comparative strength.
- Approximate/sampled metrics can be valid evidence when method identity and material uncertainty remain explicit.
- Distribution/quantile/category-share references remain purpose-driven; no universal drift/anomaly score.
- Explicit normalization can preserve a derived comparison while raw values remain non-comparable, but normalization is versioned and provenance-bearing.
- Rolling/adaptive Baselines require explicit refresh, holdout, inclusion/exclusion and version semantics.
- A current Observation must not silently redefine the reference used to judge itself.
- `Looks anomalous` alone cannot justify exclusion from history.
- Repeated bad behavior can become descriptively typical without becoming normatively acceptable.
- Multiple plausible Baselines do not receive hidden newest/largest/narrowest/broadest precedence.
- Historical Baselines and Assessments remain preserved across refresh/regime change.

Later Phase 006 rules still to be refined:

- Group 04 — thresholds/margins/warning/failure/waiver Assessment semantics — **next**;
- Group 05 — selective transformation-aware propagation/reconciliation;
- Group 06 — composite health and progressive result timing/control-suitability;
- Group 07 — consolidation/exit.

Cross-phase boundaries:

- Phase 005 decides metric/Expectation/threshold authority and disclosure governance.
- Phase 006 defines metric and health semantics.
- Phase 007 refines Lineage-aware propagation/operational use.
- Phase 009 evaluates actual source support, cost, latency and retention.
- Phase 010 selects computation/storage/fast-path architecture.

Do not recursively cascade every upstream statistic through Lineage. Do not force monitoring metrics onto the production critical path unless an explicitly accepted high-consequence control requires them and the later evidence/timing criteria are satisfied.
